course: dictionary
lesson: 5936
title: Masculine and feminine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Masculine is a word that describes qualities people often link with men or boys, such as a deep voice. It can also mean suitable for men. In grammar, «masculine» names a group of words, such as «he», «king» and «actor».
explain: In French and some other languages, every noun belongs to a group, either masculine or feminine. «Un chapeau» is a hat and «une casquette» is a cap. The small words «un» and «une» show the group, and word endings often give clues.
explain: Ideas of what is masculine change between countries and times, so do not treat them as fixed rules. Boys and girls can like any colour or hobby. Grammar gender is a label for words, not a judgement about people: «Une personne is feminine even for a man.»
fact: Masculine means having qualities people traditionally link with men or boys, or being suitable for men.
fact: In grammar, masculine is a group of words, such as «he», «king» and «actor» in English.
fact: The opposite of masculine is feminine.
fact: «Un chapeau» (a hat) is masculine, and «une casquette» (a cap) is feminine.
fact: Word endings give hints: -eau words are almost always masculine, and -ette words are almost always feminine.
exercise: Which word in this pair is masculine: «un chapeau» or «une casquette»? | la table | une casquette | *un chapeau
exercise: Which word is the masculine form? | *king | queen | princess
exercise: «Un bébé is masculine even for a baby girl.» Why is «un bébé» masculine? | Because babies are always boys | *Because the word is in the masculine group, even when the baby is a girl | Because it means a boy | Because it ends in -ette
test: Ideas of what is masculine change between countries and times. Which statement is true? | Girls can never be masculine in grammar | Only boys can like football | Masculine is the same in every country and every year | *What people see as masculine can change between countries and times
test: Which ending is almost always feminine? | -er | -eau | -ment | *-ette
exam: In French, which noun is masculine? | la table | *le livre | une personne | une casquette
